      "writtenOn": "2025-08-12T14:58:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are empty functions guaranteed not to use the stack? I can\u0027t see why they should, but maybe they could still have some compiler-generated prelude checking the stack pointer or something.\n\nI think we should instead make an exception for unit tests, something like:\n\n\"Except in unit-test-only builds for the host, the `reset_handler` function must be implemented as a naked function... \"",
      "revId": "ae718b52b4430feb7bb77858b0c250d42396c3fa",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
