      "writtenOn": "2025-08-12T18:35:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was concerned about this too. I checked several configurations on godbolt.org earlier, like enabling BTI, stack protector and using different optimization levels, etc.\nAn empty function without any parameters always resulted in a single ret instruction. If the function had a parameter and the code was compiled using -O0, it pushed the parameter to the stack just to discard it in the next instruction.\nSo by experience it should be OK, but I wasn\u0027t able to find any guarantees from the compiler\u0027s side that this will always be true.\nI am changing the safety comment to be on the safe side.",
      "parentUuid": "6c7546da_50f04f5b",
      "revId": "ae718b52b4430feb7bb77858b0c250d42396c3fa",
